{
  "version": 1,
  "mode": "location-news",
  "notes": [
    "Soft-launch source pack: free public RSS/Atom only. No paid APIs, no keys.",
    "Coverage: world, national and trade outlets so every map level (World > Country > State equivalent > City) can show its own stories. home = outlet's country; assumeHome = untagged items from a national outlet are filed to its home country; quality 1-3 feeds ranking. Location tags come from locate.js (deterministic gazetteer) at build time.",
    "Some hosts 403/429 intermittently (bot filters, WAF). Fetcher records failures and continues.",
    "Labels: hard-news = primary reporting / agency releases / discrete confirmable claims; analysis = opinion, commentary, trend pieces, explainers without a discrete confirmable claim (Works in Progress–style, Noahpinion, Asterisk, Volts, Atlantic Council briefs, Construction Physics essays, MIT News, etc.).",
    "Verification: primary=true marks the subject's own channel (agency / company press / IR): Confirmed for its own announcements and promotes matching story clusters. outlet groups feeds from one publisher (NYT feeds = one outlet) when counting independent sources.",
    "Unconfirmed = factual claim that could be confirmed by the subject/agency/company, from a non-primary outlet, not yet multi-sourced or confirmed. Do NOT park opinion/trend/commentary there. Those lack a fountainhead to confirm and belong in Analysis.",
    "Analysis classification: kind=analysis feeds are always Analysis. Additionally the fetcher/verify heuristics reclassify hard-news items whose titles match why/how/opinion/essay/the case for/trend-roundup/explainer patterns (also /opinion|/explainer|/essay URL paths). NPR Science stays hard-news for discrete events; its explainers/roundups flip via heuristics.",
    "requireTopic: general-news feeds only contribute items that classify as energy, infrastructure, industry or geopolitics (locate.js categorize).",
    "Energy sector feeds (sector: energy) were added in v24 for the Energy tab: agency releases (NRC, DOE Office of Nuclear Energy, EIA) plus trade press per source. Trade-press feeds do not assume a home country, so a story that names no place is filed worldwide. Tested and not added (box, Oct 7 2026): IEA (no public RSS, 404), Recharge (404), Hydrogen Insight (404), NEI (403), FERC (403), Mining.com (403), CleanTechnica (403), Hydrogen Fuel News (403, bot filter), S&P Global (403), Renewables Now (404), IAEA (404), NucNet (404), H2 View and Biofuels Digest (feeds return no items), World Oil (no item dates), NEI Magazine and IEEFA (stale).",
    "Sector tab feeds (v25, tested Oct 7, 2026): free RSS for Raw materials, Manufacturing, Services, Technology and Policy, marked with a sector field. Not added: 403 from the box: agriculture.com, AgWeb, USDA, Fierce Pharma, Forestry.com, Consultancy.uk, Telecoms.com, Devex, OECD. 404: FAO, Farmers Weekly, Mining Weekly, SeafoodSource, National Fisherman, The Fish Site, IndustryWeek, Assembly, C&EN, Chronicle of Philanthropy, SteelOrbis. 429: IMF, Wood Business. No items: Chemical Week, Mining Journal, The Manufacturer, World Bank news. Stale: Aerospace Technology, WHO news, FreightWaves dates."
  ],
